Bootstrap: docker
From: python:3.12-slim-trixie

%labels
    Name         ligand3d
    Description  2D molecule to minimized 3D structure
    Upstream     https://github.com/SethWoodbury/ligand3d
    Maintainer   Seth M. Woodbury

%help
    ligand3d, self-contained. The source is baked in, so this image is a
    pinned version of the tool rather than a runtime for whatever happens to
    be checked out.

        apptainer run ligand3d.sif build "O=C1CN2CCC1CC2" -o quin.cif
        apptainer run ligand3d.sif doctor
        apptainer run ligand3d.sif --help

    Included: MMFF94, UFF, GFN-FF, GFN1, GFN2, pH protonation, offline IUPAC
    name lookup, the sketcher, Rosetta params, and the RFdiffusion4 annotated
    CIF writer.

    Not included: the neural potentials. torch alone is several gigabytes and
    the MACE and fairchem sides cannot share an environment, so those live in
    their own images. The `ligand3d` wrapper script beside this file picks the
    right image from the backend you asked for, which is the reason to use the
    wrapper rather than calling apptainer directly.

    Nested apptainer does not work, so `--container` and `--slurm` cannot be
    used from inside this image. The wrapper handles both on the host.

%post
    set -eux

    # apptainer bind-mounts $HOME during the build, so without this the
    # builder's ~/.local can shadow what is being installed here.
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1

    # libgomp1 is the OpenMP runtime. The slim base omits it, and tblite's
    # wheel bundles gfortran/blas/lapack but not that — so GFN1 and GFN2 fail
    # at import with a message about a "C extension" that names no library.
    #
    # A JRE for OPSIN, which is what makes `ligand3d fetch` resolve systematic
    # names with no network. Headless keeps it to what is actually needed.
    #
    # xtb is the standalone binary GFN-FF runs through; if the distribution
    # has no package the build continues without it and GFN-FF is simply
    # unavailable, which the self-check reports rather than fails on.
    apt-get update
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends libgomp1 default-jre-headless
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends xtb || echo "no xtb package; GFN-FF will be unavailable"
    apt-get clean
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    pip install --no-cache-dir --upgrade pip
    pip install --no-cache-dir "/opt/ligand3d-src[xtb,protonation,names]"

    # The source was only needed to build the wheel; the installed package is
    # what runs. Leaving it would invite editing a copy that has no effect.
    rm -rf /opt/ligand3d-src

    # Fail the build rather than ship an image that cannot do what it claims.
    python /opt/selfcheck.py
    rm -f /opt/selfcheck.py

%files
    . /opt/ligand3d-src
    container/selfcheck.py /opt/selfcheck.py

%environment
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
    export LANG=C.UTF-8
    # Keeps a labmate's ~/.local/lib from shadowing the pinned packages, which
    # is the whole point of freezing this.
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1

%runscript
    exec ligand3d "$@"
